// mutations.memql
//
// Write paths in the `actions` namespace (epic #1734). Phase 0 (#1735)
// ships ONE: recordActionCandidate -- the single path that records
// a captured trace as a v1:actions:candidate row.
//
// Authorization (owned tier): ownerUserId is stamped from actor.userId so
// the caller cannot land a candidate owned by someone else; the conformance
// classifier reads actor.userId in the insert body and buckets this as
// owned. Provenance: provenanceMutation is stamped with this mutation's own
// name; the engine stamps createdBy from the authenticated actor.
//
// Id handling mirrors recordHarnessObservation: candidateId is
// optional -- when omitted the engine assigns the id on insert.

// recordActionCandidate
// =============================
// Append a v1:actions:candidate trace for a completed LLM step. The
// ordered capability calls (with per-arg value provenance) and the
// resource-dependency edges are computed Go-side by the data-flow tracer
// (component/harness/actiontrace) and handed in as already-structured
// arrays; the mutation stays declarative.
// Internal write path: the harness Go side calls this after each LLM step;
// it is NOT exposed on the MCP/SDK surface (no @mcp / @sdk).
// mintAction
// ==================
// Mint a v1:actions:action (primitive) from a completed LLM step (Phase 1,
// #1736). ownerUserId is stamped from actor.userId (owned tier). The harness
// calls this after an LLM step succeeds, passing the captured replayable
// calls + the input/result fingerprints.
// Internal write path -- not on the MCP/SDK surface.
//
// EVERY @required concept field is written HERE (memql#3619). It used to write
// only two of the six that need it and leave kind / reliability /
// reinforceCount / version to "their concept @default values" -- which do not
// exist at insert time. A concept-field @default is never applied on insert
// (memql#2960), so a @required field carrying one is still unset, and this
// mutation failed JSON-schema validation on EVERY call. mintActionFromRun is
// best-effort, so the failure became a log line and the replay library never
// got a row: the whole action-minting path was dead while looking healthy.
//
// The four new stamps are CONSTANTS, not args with `??`, unlike
// sideEffectClass and status. That asymmetry is the point: sideEffectClass and
// status are computed per-mint by the caller's surface-aware trust gate, while
// kind / reliability / reinforceCount / version describe what a FRESH mint is
// by definition -- a primitive, at the starting confidence, with no verified
// replays, at version 1. Exposing them as args would let a caller mint an
// action straight at reliability 1.0 and skip the trust ladder the replay path
// leans on; reinforceAction is the only thing that may move them, and it
// computes the new values engine-side.
//
// The constants MUST track the concept's @default declarations -- the pair is
// what a reader takes as "the default", and the two disagreeing is how the
// field went unwritten in the first place.
// reinforceAction
// =======================
// Bump an action's reliability + reinforceCount after a verified successful
// replay (fingerprint match). The new values are computed engine-side (the
// MemQL parser has no arithmetic, mirroring the semanticMemory reinforce
// pattern) and handed in. update read-merges the prior row, so ownerUserId
// and the captured calls are preserved. Internal write path.
// registerSurface
// =======================
// Register (or re-version) an execution surface in the resolver's registry
// (Phase 2, #1737). ownerUserId is stamped from actor.userId (owned tier).
// The served capability verbs + availability + failover priority are the
// data the resolver binds against.
/// Register a v1:actions:surface (workbench / computer-use:<machineId> / mcp:<server>) with its
/// served capabilities + availability + failover priority. ownerUserId stamped from actor.userId
/// (owned tier). #1737.
@actor
mutate surface registerSurface {
  args {
    surfaceId    string
    slug         string!
    kind         string!
    machineId    string
    capabilities []string!
    priority     int
  }
  insert {
    accept { slug, kind, machineId, capabilities }
    stamp {
      id: args.surfaceId
      ownerUserId: actor.userId
      available: true
      priority: args.priority ?? 100
      status: "active"
      lastSeen: now
      provenanceMutation: "registerSurface"
    }
  }
}

// setSurfaceAvailability
// ==============================
// Flip a surface's availability (the failover signal) and stamp the
// heartbeat clock. update read-merges so the served capabilities + slug are
// preserved. #1737.
/// Set a v1:actions:surface availability flag (the resolver's failover signal) and refresh its
/// lastSeen heartbeat. #1737.
mutate surface setSurfaceAvailability {
  args {
    surfaceId  string!
    available  boolean!
  }
  update {
    id: args.surfaceId
    args.available
    lastSeen: now
    provenanceMutation: "setSurfaceAvailability"
  }
}

// confirmAction
// =====================
// Promote a confirm-gated candidate action to active after a human confirms
// it (Phase 4 #1739). A real-machine write/exec action mints as candidate and
// is held off the replay ladder (the active-only replay queries skip it) until
// this confirm flips it to active. update read-merges so the captured calls +
// ownerUserId are preserved. Internal write path driven by the confirm UI.
// deprecateAction
// =======================
// Deprecate an action whose reliability fell below the floor (Phase 4 #1739).
// A deprecated action is kept (append-only) but excluded from the active-only
// replay queries, so it is no longer offered. Driven by the consolidation
// decay sweep.
// decayAction
// ===================
// Set an action's decayed reliability (Phase 4 #1739). The decayed value is
// computed engine-side from lastReinforced age (the MemQL parser has no
// arithmetic, mirroring the semanticMemory decay mutation) and handed in by
// the consolidation sweep.
// bumpActionVersion
// =========================
// Bump an action's monotonic version (Phase 5 #1740). References pin by
// default, so an edited action lands a new version and existing pins stay on
// the old one until the verified upgrade migration bumps them. The new version
// value is computed engine-side (the MemQL parser has no arithmetic) and
// handed in. update read-merges so the captured calls + ownerUserId persist.
/// Bump a v1:actions:action monotonic version on edit (Phase 5 #1740; value computed engine-side).
/// Pins stay on the prior version until the verified upgrade migration moves them.
mutate action bumpActionVersion {
  args {
    actionId  string!
    version   int!
  }
  update {
    id: args.actionId
    args.version
    provenanceMutation: "bumpActionVersion"
  }
}
